hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2757","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Yahya ibn Sa'id, narrated to us Ja'far, who narrated to me his father, who said:\nWe came to Jabir ibn 'Abdullah and asked him about the Hajj of the Prophet (ﷺ). He mentioned part of the hadith, then returned to the Black Stone and touched it (istilam), then went out to al-Safa. He said, \I begin with what Allah has commanded","\"" and recited:\n*\""Indeed"," as-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah.\""* [Quran 2:158]\n\nHe then climbed al-Safa until he could see the House"," and said the takbir three times"," meaning he said:\n*\""There is no god but Allah alone"," with no partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs all praise"," and He is over all things competent. There is no god but Allah alone; He fulfills His promise"," grants victory to His servant"," and defeats the confederates alone.\""*\n\nHe repeated these words three times. Then he descended until his feet reached the valley"," where he ran (sa'y). When he climbed (the other hill)"," he walked until he reached al-Marwah. He climbed it until he could see the House"," and said as he had said on al-Safa."""
